  "Onderdeel: paginakop, werkbalk en filters": "Component: page header, toolbar and filters",
  "Page header, toolbar and filters": "",
  "Every page opens the same way: the title on top, under it a subtitle on an index page or the breadcrumb on a detail page, and the buttons to the right of the title. An index adds one toolbar: saved views on the left, the filter and the view switch on the right.": "",
  "One header, two pages": "",
  "Index page": "",
  "Showing 8 of 46 open tickets · sorted on waiting time": "",
  "Detail page": "",
  "received 4 October": "",
  "Title.": "",
  "The page or the object, 28 px bold, first in reading order. A detail page puts its type and status pills above it.": "",
  "Subtitle or breadcrumb.": "",
  "An index says what is shown against the whole: \"Showing 8 of 46\". A detail page shows the way back: list, then the object number.": "",
  "Two rows.": "",
  "Row 1 holds the title with the buttons to its right, row 2 the subtitle line over the full width, so a long subtitle runs on under the buttons. The primary action is the rightmost button, filled blue.": "",
  "Download.": "",
  "On every index. It exports what the list shows now, with the active filters, as a spreadsheet or CSV.": "",
  "buildiq.": "",
  "The orange square opens the page definition in buildiq. Icon-only, so it never competes with the real work.": "",
  "More.": "",
  "Everything rare. A detail page keeps its daily actions out here (Edit, the quick actions) and folds the rest in.": "",
  "The toolbar, with the filter panel open": "",
  "Saved views": "",
  "Past the deadline": "",
  "Type: Request": "",
